   6. AI Specific Guidance

Before inputting any information into an AI tool, Team Members must assess whether the data is appropriate for use based on its classification and
the nature of the tool.
   •   All Team Members must refer to this Data Classification Policy to determine the classification level of the data they wish to use.
   •   If needed, the Data Inventory and Classification Report contains a comprehensive list of data and their classification tier, which Team
       Members can reference
   •   They must also refer to the Artificial Intelligence Driven Tools Policy to determine whether the AI tool is a Type A Tool (where data may
       be retained, shared or used for training the algorithm for third parties) or a Type B Tool (where data sharing can be disabled or is
       contractually restricted).
   •   Input of data is only permitted if it complies with the data handling guidance for that classification level and tool type and with the Artificial
       Intelligence Driven Tools Policy.
No data may be input into any AI system unless the Team Member can confidently determine that the use aligns with Destination Vancouver’s
current data governance policies.




